   $q$Which statement best expresses a theme of the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Ordinary people's experiences are an important part of history.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Famous inventors are the most interesting people to study.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Telephones have changed a great deal since 1958.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"topic-not-theme"},{"text":"Floods were common in small towns during the 1950s.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Ordinary people's experiences are an important part of history.$q$, $q$Mr. Washington's night at the switchboard, missing from the newspaper, becomes the heart of Zainab's project. Zainab wanted to study a famous inventor at first, but the story shows her changing that view.$q$, 'draft', 'feb0921d-e7e7-5ed4-83c7-6817a1fb8590')
